1
00:00:03,054 --> 00:00:04,869
A rabbit, a dragon, a boat…

2
00:00:04,919 --> 00:00:07,148
Clouds change shape all the time.

3
00:00:07,198 --> 00:00:08,943
But what are they made of?

4
00:00:08,993 --> 00:00:10,927
And where do they come from?

5
00:00:11,722 --> 00:00:15,250
In the kitchen, Noah holds a cold lid above the pot:

6
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:16,351
fog, then drops!

7
00:00:16,401 --> 00:00:17,521
Mila has a hunch:

8
00:00:17,571 --> 00:00:19,429
could a cloud be like that?

9
00:00:20,212 --> 00:00:21,726
Discovery mission!

10
00:00:24,242 --> 00:00:24,865
Mini mode!

11
00:00:24,915 --> 00:00:26,346
The Sun warms the sea,

12
00:00:26,396 --> 00:00:28,703
lakes and rivers: water evaporates.

13
00:00:28,753 --> 00:00:31,936
It becomes vapor, invisible, mixed with the air.

14
00:00:31,986 --> 00:00:33,265
And warm air rises.

15
00:00:34,051 --> 00:00:35,636
As it rises, the air cools.

16
00:00:35,686 --> 00:00:37,938
And cold air can't hold as much vapor:

17
00:00:37,988 --> 00:00:42,470
it sticks onto tiny specks of dust and turns back into water, in droplets.

18
00:00:43,285 --> 00:00:47,130
Billions of droplets, so small and so light that they float:

19
00:00:47,180 --> 00:00:48,104
that's a cloud!

20
00:00:48,154 --> 00:00:50,312
When they grow and stick together,

21
00:00:50,362 --> 00:00:51,660
they fall: it rains.

22
00:00:52,430 --> 00:00:55,458
Inside, it's mist: drops all over the canopy!

23
00:00:55,508 --> 00:00:58,331
A cloud is almost something you can touch…

24
00:00:58,381 --> 00:00:59,544
and it's all wet.

25
00:01:00,389 --> 00:01:02,378
That's how clouds form.

26
00:01:03,875 --> 00:01:05,090
Rising air cools down,

27
00:01:05,140 --> 00:01:08,935
and its water vapor turns into billions of tiny droplets: a cloud.

28
00:01:09,832 --> 00:01:10,815
With an adult:

29
00:01:10,865 --> 00:01:13,544
hold a cold lid above a steaming pot.

30
00:01:13,594 --> 00:01:16,986
The vapor turns back into drops: a mini cloud!

31
00:01:17,751 --> 00:01:20,403
And why do snowflakes have six branches?

32
00:01:20,453 --> 00:01:21,804
The answer tomorrow.
